    <article class="main-content">

      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Our security commitment</strong>
        <p>
          LetsStudy Pro aims to provide a safe and reliable
          digital environment. We work to protect platform
          information and services through appropriate security
          practices, responsible access management and ongoing
          improvements.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="policy-section" id="overview">
        <h2>1. Overview</h2>
        <p>
          This Security Policy describes the general security
          practices and responsibilities associated with using
          LetsStudy Pro.
        </p>
        <p>
          LetsStudy Pro is a Global Digital Learning &amp; Growth
          Ecosystem designed to connect people, knowledge,
          technology, businesses and opportunities through
          integrated digital services.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy applies to our website, digital accounts,
          learning services, resources, business services,
          marketplace features and other platform functions
          where applicable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="principles">
        <h2>2. Security Principles</h2>
        <p>
          Our security approach is guided by the following
          principles:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Confidentiality:</strong> Protecting information from unauthorized access or disclosure.</li>
          <li><strong>Integrity:</strong> Reducing unauthorized changes to information and platform records.</li>
          <li><strong>Availability:</strong> Supporting reliable access to our services.</li>
          <li><strong>Access control:</strong> Restricting protected functions to authorized users.</li>
          <li><strong>Accountability:</strong> Encouraging responsible use and appropriate security oversight.</li>
          <li><strong>Continuous improvement:</strong> Reviewing and improving security practices as our platform evolves.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="accounts">
        <h2>3. Account Security</h2>
        <p>
          Users are responsible for protecting their accounts
          and authentication credentials.
        </p>
        <p>We recommend that users:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Create strong and unique passwords.</li>
          <li>Never share passwords, verification codes or recovery credentials.</li>
          <li>Keep their registered email address secure.</li>
          <li>Use available account recovery and verification features responsibly.</li>
          <li>Sign out after using shared or public devices.</li>
          <li>Review account activity where such information is available.</li>
          <li>Report suspected unauthorized access promptly.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          LetsStudy Pro may provide authentication, password
          recovery, email verification and other account
          protection features depending on the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="information">
        <h2>4. Information Protection</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to protect information handled by our services
          using reasonable technical and organizational safeguards.
        </p>
        <p>Depending on the service and data involved, measures may include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>HTTPS encryption for supported website connections.</li>
          <li>Authentication and authorization controls.</li>
          <li>Database access restrictions and security rules.</li>
          <li>Appropriate handling of account information.</li>
          <li>Restricted access to administrative information.</li>
          <li>Maintenance and updates to supported platform components.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We seek to limit access to personal and operational
          information to legitimate purposes and authorized
          activities.
        </p>
        <p>
          Details about personal information collection,
          processing and retention are explained in our
          <a href="privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="firebase">
        <h2>5. Platform Infrastructure and Technology</h2>
        <p>
          LetsStudy Pro may use cloud hosting, authentication,
          databases and other technology services to operate
          its digital ecosystem.
        </p>
        <p>
          These technologies may include Google Firebase and
          associated Google Cloud services.
        </p>
        <p>
          Appropriate configuration of these services is
          important for platform security. Depending on the
          feature, this may involve:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Firebase Authentication for supported sign-in functions.</li>
          <li>Firestore Security Rules for database access control.</li>
          <li>Hosting configuration and HTTPS support.</li>
          <li>Restricted administrative operations.</li>
          <li>Secure management of privileged credentials.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Public website code and Firebase client configuration
          are not substitutes for server-side authorization.
          Sensitive operations must be protected through
          appropriate security rules or trusted backend services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="admin">
        <h2>6. Administrative Security</h2>
        <p>
          Administrative features are intended for authorized
          personnel. Administrative access should be limited
          according to assigned responsibilities.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Administrative accounts should use secure credentials.</li>
          <li>Restricted operations should require appropriate authorization.</li>
          <li>Administrative permissions should be granted carefully.</li>
          <li>Privileged credentials and secret keys must not be published in client-side code.</li>
          <li>Important administrative changes should be appropriately controlled.</li>
          <li>Access should be reviewed when responsibilities change.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A user interface that hides administrative controls
          does not provide sufficient security by itself.
          Authorization must also be enforced by the relevant
          backend or database security configuration.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="payments">
        <h2>7. Payments and Transactions</h2>
        <p>
          Where payment, subscription, wallet or marketplace
          functions are available, users should verify transaction
          details before confirming an action.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use only payment methods and channels officially provided or identified by the platform.</li>
          <li>Do not share payment passwords, PINs or one-time verification codes.</li>
          <li>Report suspicious payment requests or transaction activity.</li>
          <li>Keep relevant transaction confirmations for reference.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Payment processing may depend on external payment
          providers. Their own terms and security procedures
          may apply.
        </p>
        <p>
          Users should not assume that a displayed wallet balance
          or transaction message is proof of a completed payment
          unless the relevant transaction has been verified.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="third-party">
        <h2>8. Third-Party Services and External Links</h2>
        <p>
          Our ecosystem may contain links, integrations,
          embedded content or services operated by third parties.
        </p>
        <p>
          These external services may have separate security
          practices, privacy policies and terms of use.
          LetsStudy Pro does not control every external website
          or service.
        </p>
        <p>
          Users should verify website addresses and exercise
          caution before submitting personal information to
          external platforms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="responsibilities">
        <h2>9. User Security Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          All users are expected to use LetsStudy Pro responsibly.
          Users must not:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Attempt unauthorized access to accounts, databases or systems.</li>
          <li>Bypass authentication or access restrictions.</li>
          <li>Exploit vulnerabilities without authorization.</li>
          <li>Upload malicious software or harmful code.</li>
          <li>Interfere with the availability or operation of services.</li>
          <li>Access, copy or disclose another person's private information without authorization.</li>
          <li>Use the platform to distribute phishing links or fraudulent content.</li>
          <li>Impersonate platform administrators or other users.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Security-related misuse may result in investigation
          and appropriate action under our
          <a href="acceptable-use.html">Acceptable Use Policy</a>
          and applicable laws.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="incidents">
        <h2>10. Security Incident Reporting</h2>
        <p>
          Users should notify LetsStudy Pro if they discover
          suspicious account activity, suspected unauthorized
          access, exposed information or another potential
          security incident involving our platform.
        </p>
        <p>
          A useful incident report may include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>A description of what happened.</li>
          <li>The affected page, feature or service.</li>
          <li>The approximate date and time.</li>
          <li>The potential impact, if known.</li>
          <li>Relevant screenshots or non-sensitive evidence.</li>
          <li>Contact information for follow-up.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Never send passwords, authentication codes, private
          keys or other secret credentials in a security report.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="disclosure">
        <h2>11. Responsible Vulnerability Disclosure</h2>
        <p>
          We encourage responsible reporting of genuine security
          concerns affecting LetsStudy Pro.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you believe you have discovered a vulnerability:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Report it privately using our official contact email.</li>
          <li>Provide enough information for us to understand the issue.
          
          <li>Provide enough information for us to understand the issue.</li>
          <li>Avoid accessing, modifying or downloading information belonging to other users.</li>
          <li>Do not disrupt platform services or conduct destructive security testing.</li>
          <li>Allow reasonable time for investigation before public disclosure.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Submitting a vulnerability report does not automatically
          create an employment, contractual or reward arrangement.
          Any additional arrangement must be expressly confirmed
          by LetsStudy Pro.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="limitations">
        <h2>12. Security Limitations</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to support the security of
          our platform. However, no website, application,
          network or electronic storage system can be guaranteed
          to be completely secure.
        </p>
        <p>
          Security incidents may arise from technical failures,
          third-party services, compromised devices, user
          negligence or threats beyond our reasonable control.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by applicable law, LetsStudy Pro
          does not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation
          or absolute protection against every cyber threat.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section" id="updates">
        <h2>13. Policy Updates</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Security Policy to reflect changes
          in our technology, services, operational practices
          or applicable requirements.
        </p>
        <p>
          The latest version will be published on this page.
          Continued use of the platform after an update is
          subject to the applicable policies and requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

